course: dictionary
lesson: 13400
title: A house for hens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A henhouse is a small hut or shed where hens live. Hens sleep there at night and lay their eggs there too, so it is their home on a farm or in a garden.
explain: Look at the two parts of the word: hen and house. A hen is a female chicken, and a house is a place to live, so a henhouse is a house for hens. «Every evening, Grandad shuts the henhouse door to keep the hens safe.» The clue is the word shuts: the hens are kept inside.
explain: A henhouse can also appear in a phrase. «Keep an eye out, because there is a fox in the henhouse!» Here the fox is the danger, and it is inside the place that should be safe. Context helps you see that this phrase means something more than a real fox.
fact: A henhouse is a small hut or shed for hens.
fact: Hens sleep in a henhouse to stay safe from foxes.
fact: Hens also lay their eggs in a henhouse.
fact: «Henhouse» is a noun, and its plural is «henhouses».
fact: «A fox in the henhouse» means danger is inside a place that should be safe.
exercise: «The hens went into the henhouse before dark.» Where did the hens go? | To the school | *To the henhouse | To the river | To the shop
exercise: Farmer Eve has 6 hens in her henhouse, and each hen lays 1 egg a day. How many eggs are laid in one day? | 60 | 1 | 12 | *6
exercise: Dad says, «There is a fox in the henhouse!» What does he mean? | The hens are having a party | A fox is a good friend of the hens | The henhouse is empty | *Danger is inside a place that should be safe
test: «The hens lay eggs in the henhouse every morning.» Where are the eggs laid? | *In the henhouse | In a box at school | In the sea | Under the bed
test: «Shut the henhouse door before the fox comes.» What is a henhouse? | *A small hut or shed where hens live | A pond for ducks | A big house for people | A bag for carrying eggs
exam: Which sentence uses henhouse correctly? | We ate the henhouse for lunch. | *The hens slept in the henhouse. | The henhouse is a fast train. | He drove his henhouse to school.
